{
  // Typechecks the TEST tree as well as src (ARCHITECTURE → "Build and test
  // resolution", rule 5). Three constraints, all measured — none is a style
  // choice:
  //
  //  1. Extends `tsconfig.base.json` DIRECTLY, not the package `tsconfig.json`.
  //     `extends` cannot *unset* an inherited value, so the package config's
  //     `rootDir: "src"` would survive and every cross-package `paths` file
  //     below it becomes TS6059 ("not under rootDir").
  //  2. Declares `paths` mapping `@dagsocial/*` to the sibling's `src/index.ts`,
  //     mirroring the vitest alias. Without it `tsc` follows `exports` to the
  //     sibling's `dist` types — the stale-`dist` class rule 5 exists to kill,
  //     and the suite would be checked against types it never executes.
  //  3. No `types: ["vitest/globals"]`. The conclusion is right; the premise
  //     recorded here was FALSE and is corrected. It read "measured: no test
  //     file uses bare globals, every one imports from 'vitest' explicitly" —
  //     but `test/config.test.ts:44` called `vi.resetModules()` while importing
  //     only `{describe, it, expect, beforeEach}`, and compiling this tree
  //     reported exactly one `TS2304: Cannot find name 'vi'` for it. The remedy
  //     was to add that one import (done), NOT to admit an ambient global,
  //     which would license the drift the explicit-import convention prevents
  //     (ARCHITECTURE rule 5). Now measured true: every test file imports what
  //     it uses, and this config is wired into `typecheck` at zero errors.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "paths": {
      "@dagsocial/*": ["../*/src/index.ts"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src", "test"]
}
